{"weights_commit":"16b6a1c","summary":"Version 1 passes 1 of its 4 checks, so it does not pass its own test yet. Known Mars analogs beat ordinary places: 56% of pairs (pass mark 80%). Known Mars analogs beat plain deserts: 33% of pairs (pass mark 60%). Polar and highland analogs beat ordinary places: 45% of pairs (pass mark 80%). Basalt and crater sites beat ordinary places on terrain: 84% of pairs (pass mark 80%). Most misses are small, rugged or icy analogs that fill only part of a 50 km cell, or polar sites whose cold matches but whose small day-to-night swing, low sun and clear air do not match Jezero. We publish the result as it came out; the weights and pass marks were fixed before the run.","not_blind_note":"This is not a blind first run. A throwaway prototype scored the same test places twice on 14 November, and two lessons from it shaped this version. The weights and pass marks below were committed before this run, and the places marked blind had never been scored before.","prototype_runs":[{"date":"2026-11-14","result":"Moon: 67% against a pass mark of 80%"},{"date":"2026-11-14","result":"Mars: 79% against 80% (ordinary places) and 54% against 60% (plain deserts)"}],"tests":[{"id":"mars","title":"Mars test","body":"mars","plain":"Known Mars analogs should beat ordinary places and plain deserts. Each place is scored on its 0.5° cell against Jezero crater, with every scored challenge weighted equally (a weighted geometric mean of the challenge scores, under the same 70% data rule as the map). A pair counts as a win when the analog scores higher; ties count half.","groups":[{"id":"mars-analog","name":"Known Mars analogs","plain":"Places already used to test Mars missions."},{"id":"ordinary","name":"Ordinary places","plain":"Farmland, forest and cities that nobody uses as an analog."},{"id":"desert","name":"Plain deserts","plain":"Big deserts that aren't analogs. They catch a method that only rewards dry, bare ground."}],"places":[{"id":"haughton-crater-devon-island","name":"Haughton crater, Devon Island","lat":75.38,"lon":-89.67,"group":"mars-analog","cell":3095,"score":0.3196,"land_rank":0.2018,"best_target":"mars-jezero","held_out":true,"blind":false},{"id":"yungay-atacama","name":"Yungay, Atacama","lat":-24.0804,"lon":-69.9412,"group":"mars-analog","cell":62291,"score":0.542,"land_rank":0.8118,"best_target":"mars-jezero","held_out":true,"blind":false},{"id":"mcmurdo-dry-valleys","name":"McMurdo Dry Valleys","lat":-77.47,"lon":162.52,"group":"mars-analog","cell":75358,"score":0.2691,"land_rank":0.1262,"best_target":"mars-jezero","held_out":true,"blind":false},{"id":"gypsum-hill-axel-heiberg","name":"Gypsum Hill, Axel Heiberg","lat":79.4,"lon":-90.75,"group":"mars-analog","cell":1341,"score":0.2101,"land_rank":0.0621,"best_target":"mars-jezero","held_out":true,"blind":false},{"id":"bockfjorden-svalbard","name":"Bockfjorden, Svalbard","lat":79.43,"lon":13.33,"group":"mars-analog","cell":1480,"score":0.1609,"land_rank":0.0165,"best_target":"mars-jezero","held_out":false,"blind":false},{"id":"rio-tinto","name":"Rio Tinto","lat":37.683,"lon":-6.583,"group":"mars-analog","cell":35140,"score":0.4804,"land_rank":0.6791,"best_target":"mars-jezero","held_out":false,"blind":false},{"id":"mdrs-utah","name":"MDRS, Utah","lat":38.41,"lon":-110.79,"group":"mars-analog","cell":34736,"score":0.5771,"land_rank":0.8606,"best_target":"mars-jezero","held_out":false,"blind":false},{"id":"qaidam-dalangtan","name":"Qaidam (Dalangtan)","lat":38.33,"lon":91.67,"group":"mars-analog","cell":34968,"score":0.7801,"land_rank":1.0,"best_target":"mars-jezero","held_out":true,"blind":false},{"id":"tso-kar","name":"Tso Kar","lat":33.3,"lon":77.98,"group":"mars-analog","cell":38149,"score":0.446,"land_rank":0.5614,"best_target":"mars-jezero","held_out":true,"blind":false},{"id":"puga-valley","name":"Puga Valley","lat":33.2276,"lon":78.3064,"group":"mars-analog","cell":38150,"score":0.4146,"land_rank":0.4477,"best_target":"mars-jezero","held_out":false,"