o","held_out":false,"blind":false},{"id":"kalahari","name":"Kalahari","lat":-23.0,"lon":22.0,"group":"desert","cell":62000,"score":0.4487,"land_rank":0.5719,"best_target":"mars-jezero","held_out":false,"blind":false}],"checks":[{"name":"Known Mars analogs beat ordinary places","pass_mark":0.8,"result":0.556,"passed":false,"n_pairs":448,"held_out_only":0.486,"blind_only":0.762},{"name":"Known Mars analogs beat plain deserts","pass_mark":0.6,"result":0.333,"passed":false,"n_pairs":168,"held_out_only":0.308,"blind_only":0.5}],"misses":[{"place":"haughton-crater-devon-island","why":"Arctic: a small day-to-night swing, a low sun and clear air, far from Jezero. Polar air also reads as wet on the aridity index because so little water can evaporate. Lowest trait ranks: noon sun height 0.06, day-to-night swing (air) 0.06, dryness (aridity index) 0.12."},{"place":"mcmurdo-dry-valleys","why":"The valleys are smaller than a 0.5° cell, and the cell is mostly ice sheet. Polar air reads as wet on the aridity index because so little water can evaporate, and its sun is low. Lowest trait ranks: noon sun height 0.04, dust in the air 0.05, day-to-night swing (air) 0.06; 96% of the cell is permanent ice."},{"place":"gypsum-hill-axel-heiberg","why":"High Arctic: steep ground, a tiny day-to-night swing and a low sun. Lowest trait ranks: day-to-night swing (air) 0.03, noon sun height 0.03, height range 0.04."},{"place":"bockfjorden-svalbard","why":"Most of its cell is glacier, its day-to-night swing is tiny and polar air reads as wet on the aridity index. Lowest trait ranks: day-to-night swing (air) 0.01, dryness (aridity index) 0.02, noon sun height 0.03; 76% of the cell is permanent ice."},{"place":"puga-valley","why":"It sits in a steep Himalayan valley: almost all land on Earth is flatter. Lowest trait ranks: height range 0.02, ground under 10° 0.03, typical slope 0.03."},{"place":"kangerlussuaq","why":"Its ground is rough, its sun is low and its air is clear, all far from Jezero. Lowest trait ranks: height range 0.09, ground under 10° 0.11, typical slope 0.12."},{"place":"pavilion-lake","why":"Its cell is steep valley country, and EMIT has no mineral data there. Lowest trait ranks: height range 0.01, ground under 10° 0.05, typical slope 0.05."},{"place":"spotted-lake","why":"Its cell is steep valley country, and EMIT has no mineral data there, so the lake's salts can't count. Lowest trait ranks: height range 0.04, typical slope 0.05, ground under 10° 0.05."},{"place":"gros-morne","why":"A wet, rugged coast with a small day-to-night swing. Lowest trait ranks: dryness (aridity index) 0.08, typical slope 0.16, ground under 10° 0.17."},{"place":"argentine-puna","why":"The point stands for a whole high plateau, with far more height range than Jezero's floor and clear mountain air. Lowest trait ranks: height range 0.07, dust in the air 0.12, ground under 10° 0.16."},{"place":"kilauea-iki","why":"Half of its cell is sea, and the tropical climate is warm with a small day-to-night swing. Lowest trait ranks: day-to-night swing (air) 0.01, coldest ground temperature 0.06, height range 0.07."},{"place":"bletterbach","why":"An Alpine gorge: steep, high-relief ground in a mostly green cell. Lowest trait ranks: height range 0.01, typical slope 0.03, ground under 10° 0.04."},{"place":"chill-ice-lava-tube","why":"Iceland's cool, wet climate has a small day-to-night swing; the lava tube itself can't be seen by any trait. Lowest trait ranks: dryness (aridity index) 0.03, day-to-night swing (air) 0.11, height range 0.14."},{"place":"arkaroola","why":"Its hills are far rougher than Jezero's flat crater floor, and its air is clearer than Jezero's dusty sky. Lowest trait ranks: dust in the air 0.15, height range 0.22, ground under 10° 0.24."},{"place":"don-juan-pond","why":"Not ranked: the pond sits on an Antarctic cell with no aridity value (ice sheet) and no EMIT minerals, so under 70% of the weight has data. Lowest trait ranks: height range 0.02, noon sun height 0.04, dust in the air 0.05; 86% of the cell is permanent ice."}]},{"id":"moon-polar","title":"Moon test, part 1","body":"moon","plain":"Polar and highland analogs should beat ordinary places. It's a small group, and we say so. Each place is scored on its 0.5° cell against the Moon's south pole, with every scored challenge weighted equally (a weighted geometric mean of the challenge scores, under the same 70% data rule as the map). A pair counts as a win when the analog scores higher; ties count half.","groups":[{"id":"moon-analog","name":"Polar and highland Moon analogs","plain":"Places used to train for the Moon's highlands and poles."},{"id":"ordinary","name":"Ordinary places","plain":"Farmland, forest and cities that nobody uses as an analog."}],"places":[{"id":"mistastin-crater","name":"Mistastin crater","lat":55.8863,"lon":-63.3283,"group":"moon-analog","cell":20743,"score":0.4462,"land_rank":0.5216,"best_target":"moon-south-pole","held_out":true,"blind":false},{"id":"haughton-crater-devon-island","name":"Haughton crater, Devon Island","lat":75.38,"lon":-89.67,"group":"moon-analog","cell":3095,"score":0.5001,"land_rank":0.6951,"best_target":"moon-south-pole","held_out":true,"blind":false},{"id":"lofoten","name":"Lofoten","lat":68.1,"lon":13.3,"group":"moon-analog","cell":8096,"score":0.1248,"land_rank":0.0189,"best_target":"moon-south-pole","held_out":false,"blind":false},{"id":"stillwater-complex","name":"Stillwater Complex","lat":45.3894,"lon":-109.875,"group":"moon-analog","cell":29725,"score":0.3966,"land_rank":0.3948,"best_target":"moon-south-pole","held_out":false,"blind":true},{"id":"iowa-corn-belt","name":"Iowa corn belt","lat":42.0,"lon":-93.5,"group":"ordinary","cell":32365,"score":0.5582,"land_rank":0.8306,"best_target":"moon-south-pole","held_out":false,"blind":false},{"id":"beauce","name":"Beauce","lat":48.2,"lon":1.7,"group":"ordinary","cell":27362,"score":0.4699,"land_rank":0.5938,"best_target":"moon-south-pole","held_out":false,"blind":false},{"id